//- /public — the boards anybody may open.
//- Design: docs/Features/Page/Public.md, which is the Table page design
//- (docs/Features/Page/Table.md).
//-
//- The whole page is the shared table. It used to render `boardList`, the All
//- Boards page, with its query swapped for `{ permission: 'public' }` — which
//- brought the Starred/Templates/Remaining menu, the workspaces tree, the org and
//- team filters, Multi-Selection with its archive and duplicate actions, board
//- dragging and an "Add board" tile along with it, none of which means anything
//- for a list of somebody else's public boards.
template(name="publicBoards")
  .wrapper.public-boards
    +tablePage(tablePageData)

//- One row. It supplies a rowTemplate — rather than a text-cell column spec —
//- because a row is a LINK and carries its board's colours, neither of which a
//- text cell can express. It is still read-only: one anchor, no control, and
//- nothing on it changes anything.
//-
//- The cells must match the header, in order: Board, Description.
template(name="publicBoardRow")
  tr.public-board-row.js-open-public-board(
    class="{{colorClass}}"
    data-board-id="{{_id}}"
    style="{{backgroundStyle}}")
    td.public-board-title
      a.js-open-public-board-link(href="{{pathFor 'board' id=_id slug=slug}}")
        +viewer
          = title
    td.public-board-desc
      +viewer
        = description
